## Running the server

All of these wrap `docker compose`. The `docker-compose.yml` at the project root
defines the `fastmcp` service (and the Inspector behind the `dev` profile).

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `dude up --build` | Build the image and start the server (streamable HTTP on `:8000`) |
| `dude up` | Start the server (detached) |
| `dude down` | Stop and remove containers |
| `dude logs` | Follow logs for all services |
| `dude logs fastmcp` | Follow logs for the server |
| `dude shell` | Open a shell in the `fastmcp` container (default service) |

Re-run `dude up --build` whenever you change the `Dockerfile` or `pyproject.toml`.

To connect a client (Inspector, Claude Desktop, Claude Code), see
[Connecting a client](connect.md).

